WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:03.736
It was a quiet morning in the mountains near Metro City.

2
00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:08.226
Kaboom! An explosion sent dirt and rocks flying.

3
00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:12.468
When the dust settled, a construction worker peeked out from behind a boulder.

4
00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:15.640
"All clear!" she yelled.

5
00:00:15.641 --> 00:00:19.454
"All clear!" other workers yelled.

6
00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:22.424
More workers came out from behind trees and boulders.

7
00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:25.855
They carried shovels and pickaxes.

8
00:00:25.856 --> 00:00:30.305
The workers were building a new road on the side of a mountain.

9
00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:32.393
Everyone approached the blast area.

10
00:00:32.394 --> 00:00:35.459
It was now a flat surface littered with broken rocks.

11
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.075
A rock wall rose above the area.

12
00:00:38.076 --> 00:00:41.707
"Let's move these rocks out of the way," the woman said.

13
00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:46.511
"You got it, Beth!" A worker climbed into a bulldozer.

14
00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:50.689
Brumm! Brumm!

15
00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:53.192
Another worker stared at the rock wall.

16
00:00:53.193 --> 00:00:54.723
There were holes in the rock.

17
00:00:54.724 --> 00:00:57.144
Something sparkled from within.

18
00:00:57.145 --> 00:01:00.694
"Something's behind that rock wall," he said.

19
00:01:00.695 --> 00:01:02.322
"It looks like metal."

20
00:01:02.323 --> 00:01:05.983
"Stop the bulldozer!"

21
00:01:05.984 --> 00:01:08.047
Beth took a closer look.

22
00:01:08.048 --> 00:01:12.011
"You're right, Phil. Let's see what it is."

23
00:01:12.012 --> 00:01:16.591
Pickaxes swung as the workers chipped away at the rock.

24
00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:20.486
Soon a huge bronze door was revealed.

25
00:01:20.487 --> 00:01:24.499
Phil whistled. "It's big enough for a giant!"

26
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.975
"I wonder who made it," Beth said.

27
00:01:26.976 --> 00:01:28.801
Phil stepped closer.

28
00:01:28.802 --> 00:01:32.282
"And what's on the other side?" He knocked.

29
00:01:32.283 --> 00:01:36.571
"Ouch!" Phil shook his hand and then rubbed his knuckles.

30
00:01:36.572 --> 00:01:39.676
"That door must be really thick!"

31
00:01:39.677 --> 00:01:42.527
"Well, there's no answer," another worker said.

32
00:01:42.528 --> 00:01:43.722
"I guess no one's—"

33
00:01:43.723 --> 00:01:47.432
Rumble! Rumble! The mountain shook!

34
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:50.935
Phil lost his balance. "Oof!"

35
00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:55.598
Then . . . Roar! The huge door rattled!

36
00:01:55.599 --> 00:01:57.618
Dust fell from its hinges.

37
00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:04.226
Beth gulped. "Someone is home! Run!"

38
00:02:04.227 --> 00:02:06.661
*** "Okay, Roxy," Mara

39
00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:11.635
said. "What would you buy if you had a million dollars?"

40
00:02:11.636 --> 00:02:14.392
It was morning at Metro City Elementary School.

41
00:02:14.393 --> 00:02:18.320
Roxy and her friends were playing basketball before school started.

42
00:02:18.321 --> 00:02:24.148
"I don't know." Roxy took a shot and missed.

43
00:02:24.149 --> 00:02:26.826
"Maybe I'd buy a swimming pool."

44
00:02:26.827 --> 00:02:28.895
The ball bounced to Terrell.

45
00:02:28.896 --> 00:02:33.226
"You don't need a million dollars to buy a swimming pool," he said.

46
00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:36.209
He tried to take a shot, but Jack blocked him.

47
00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.746
Terrell passed the ball to Mara.

48
00:02:38.747 --> 00:02:42.291
"I wish you did have a pool, Roxy," Jack said.

49
00:02:42.292 --> 00:02:45.709
"I'd live at your house—just like Terrell."

50
00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:49.227
"Terrell's only staying with Roxy for two weeks, Jack."

51
00:02:49.228 --> 00:02:53.992
Mara dribbled past Roxy. "He doesn't live there."

52
00:02:53.993 --> 00:02:56.122
Jack stole the ball from Mara.

53
00:02:56.123 --> 00:02:58.614
"Hey!" Mara frowned.

54
00:02:58.615 --> 00:03:02.772
"What would you do with a million dollars, Jack?" Roxy asked.

55
00:03:02.773 --> 00:03:08.090
Jack took a shot and scored. "I'd buy a Jet Ski."

56
00:03:08.091 --> 00:03:09.849
Terrell rolled his eyes.

57
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:13.930
"You don't need a million dollars to buy a Jet Ski either."

58
00:03:13.931 --> 00:03:18.366
"You do if it's a flying Jet Ski," Jack said.

59
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:21.576
Everyone laughed.

60
00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:23.541
Then Roxy's watch beeped.

61
00:03:23.542 --> 00:03:25.482
She glanced at her friends.

62
00:03:25.483 --> 00:03:30.179
"I'll be right back. I'm . . . thirsty."

63
00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.544
She stepped away and opened her watch.

64
00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:36.537
"Hey, Mayor," Roxy said. "Is everything okay?"

65
00:03:36.538 --> 00:03:39.542
"We might have a problem," Mayor Bloom said.

66
00:03:39.543 --> 00:03:42.349
"Workers are building a new road in the mountains.

67
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:45.992
They blasted some rock and discovered something strange."

68
00:03:45.993 --> 00:03:48.669
"What is it?" Roxy asked.

69
00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:52.261
"It's a big door," the mayor said.

70
00:03:52.262 --> 00:03:55.631
Roxy scratched her head. "Did they open it?"

71
00:03:55.632 --> 00:03:57.749
"No," Mayor Bloom said.

72
00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.668
"But something is behind it.

73
00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:04.388
Whatever it is, it made the whole mountain shake!"

74
00:04:04.389 --> 00:04:07.062
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

75
00:04:07.063 --> 00:04:10.867
"I'm on my way!"

